  "body": "Closes #7957 and #9757\n\n### Mini-explainer for TAG review / blink-dev purposes:\nThe showPicker() method is a new addition to HTMLSelectElement which addresses a [common request from web developers](https://www.google.com/search?q=programmatically+open+select+site%3Astackoverflow.com): programmatically showing the option picker UI for a select element\n\n```html\n<select id=\"select\">\n  <option>Item 1</option>\n  <option>Item 2</option>\n</select>\n<button onclick=\"select.showPicker()\">Show the select option picker</button>\n```\n\nIn today's browsers there's currently no way to programatically open a select element. This spec adds a new method to a select element to make that possible, following in the footsteps of the `showPicker()` method added to HTMLInputElement.\n\nshowPicker() is specified with a few restrictions to improve security:\n\nIt can only be called with transient user activation. If called without, it will throw a \"NotAllowedError\" DOMException. (This is the same as how it behaves on inputs.)\n\nIt can only be called in same-origin iframes. If called in a cross-origin iframe, it will throw a \"SecurityError\" DOMException.\n\n<!--\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n-->\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Gecko\n   * Chromium (https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9754#issuecomment-1747137961)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/42091 - tests user gesture, mutability and same-origin requirements.\n   * Actually showing the picker is not testable in WPT\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1485010\n   * Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1854112\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=261814\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed:\n   * https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/20852 MDN Browser Compat Data PR\n   * https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/29406 MDN Content PR\n\n- Standards Positions:\n  - Gecko: https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/886\n  - WebKit: https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/258\n  - Chromium: https://chromestatus.com/feature/5111537299881984\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9754/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 8, 2023, 8:49 AM UTC (953c3fe)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9754/43859d4...953c3fe/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 8, 2023, 8:49 AM UTC (953c3fe)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9754/form-elements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 8, 2023, 8:49 AM UTC (953c3fe)\">/form-elements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9754/43859d4...953c3fe/form-elements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 8, 2023, 8:49 AM UTC (953c3fe)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9754/input.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 8, 2023, 8:49 AM UTC (953c3fe)\">/input.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9754/43859d4...953c3fe/input.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 8, 2023, 8:49 AM UTC (953c3fe)\">diff</a> )",
